IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `crtpa-nouns`
IMPORT `crtpa-s2-right`

-- Tests for section 2.  Every expected value is written from the text of s 2, with the reason beside it,
-- before the module was run.  In each call the inputs are, in order, those of the rule's GIVEN.

§ `Tests -- s 2(1): the person is a third party; the two routes`

-- "a person who is not a party to a contract (called in this Act a third party)"
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the person is a third party` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the person is a third party` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a): the contract expressly provides that the third party may.
#ASSERT `s 2(1)(a) the contract expressly provides that the third party may enforce the term` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1)(a) the contract expressly provides that the third party may enforce the term` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- (2): the parties did not intend the term to be enforceable -- it appears (yes), it does not appear (no), not stated.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) subsection (1)(b) does not apply to the term` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) subsection (1)(b) does not apply to the term` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) subsection (1)(b) does not apply to the term` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1)(b), subject to (2): a benefit conferred, and no intention against enforcement.
#ASSERT `s 2(1)(b) the term purports to confer a benefit on the third party and subsection (2) does not take it out` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1)(b) the term purports to confer a benefit on the third party and subsection (2) does not take it out` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1)(b) the term purports to confer a benefit on the third party and subsection (2) does not take it out` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(1)(b) the term purports to confer a benefit on the third party and subsection (2) does not take it out` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1)(b) the term purports to confer a benefit on the third party and subsection (2) does not take it out` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No benefit conferred: (b) fails whatever the judgment of s 2(2) would be.
#ASSERT `s 2(1)(b) the term purports to confer a benefit on the third party and subsection (2) does not take it out` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 2(1) as a whole: inputs are: is a party; (a); benefit conferred; the (2) judgment.
-- not a party, (a) made out: may enforce, whatever (b) says and even if the (2) judgment is against.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the third party may in the third party's own right enforce the term of the contract` FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the third party may in the third party's own right enforce the term of the contract` FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the third party may in the third party's own right enforce the term of the contract` FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the third party may in the third party's own right enforce the term of the contract` FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not a party, (a) not made out, route (b) made out.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the third party may in the third party's own right enforce the term of the contract` FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) not made out and (b) taken out by s 2(2): neither route holds.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the third party may in the third party's own right enforce the term of the contract` FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- neither route: no express provision and no benefit.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the third party may in the third party's own right enforce the term of the contract` FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the third party may in the third party's own right enforce the term of the contract` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a) not made out, a benefit conferred, and the s 2(2) judgment not stated: not answered.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the third party may in the third party's own right enforce the term of the contract` FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- a party to the contract is not a third party, so s 2(1) gives nothing, whatever the routes.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the third party may in the third party's own right enforce the term of the contract` TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the third party may in the third party's own right enforce the term of the contract` TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- s 2(3): identification`

#ASSERT `s 2(3) the third party is expressly identified in the contract by name, as a member of a class or as answering a particular description` `expressly, by name` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the third party is expressly identified in the contract by name, as a member of a class or as answering a particular description` `expressly, as a member of a class` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the third party is expressly identified in the contract by name, as a member of a class or as answering a particular description` `expressly, as answering a particular description` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the third party is expressly identified in the contract by name, as a member of a class or as answering a particular description` `by implication only` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the third party is expressly identified in the contract by name, as a member of a class or as answering a particular description` `not identified at all` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "but need not be in existence when the contract is entered into": existence is not required either way.
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the third party must be in existence when the contract is entered into` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the third party must be in existence when the contract is entered into` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- s 2(4): subject to the other relevant terms of the contract`

#ASSERT `s 2(4) section 2 confers a right on the third party to enforce the term otherwise than subject to and in accordance with the other relevant terms of the contract` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(4) section 2 confers a right on the third party to enforce the term otherwise than subject to and in accordance with the other relevant terms of the contract` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 2(5): remedies`

-- inputs: the third party has the right (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING); the remedy would have been available to a party.
#ASSERT `s 2(5) the remedy is available to the third party` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(5) the remedy is available to the third party` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(5) the remedy is available to the third party` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(5) the remedy is available to the third party` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(and the rules relating to damages, injunctions, specific performance and other remedy apply accordingly)": part of the grant for the purpose of exercising a third party's right.
#ASSERT `s 2(5) the rules relating to damages, injunctions, specific performance and other remedy apply to the third party's remedy accordingly` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(5) the rules relating to damages, injunctions, specific performance and other remedy apply to the third party's remedy accordingly` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(5) the rules relating to damages, injunctions, specific performance and other remedy apply to the third party's remedy accordingly` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- "must not be refused on the ground that, as against the promisor, the third party is a volunteer"
#ASSERT `s 2(5) the remedy may be refused on the ground that, as against the promisor, the third party is a volunteer` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(5) the remedy may be refused on the ground that, as against the promisor, the third party is a volunteer` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 2(6): terms that exclude or limit liability`

#ASSERT `s 2(6) references in this Act to the third party enforcing the term are to be construed as references to availing of the exclusion or limitation` `a term that excludes or limits liability in relation to a matter` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(6) references in this Act to the third party enforcing the term are to be construed as references to availing of the exclusion or limitation` `any other term` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(6) what a reference to the third party enforcing the term is construed as` `a term that excludes or limits liability in relation to a matter` EQUALS JUST `availing of the exclusion or limitation`
#ASSERT `s 2(6) what a reference to the third party enforcing the term is construed as` `any other term` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 2(7): promisee and promisor`

-- inputs: the term is enforceable by a third party; where the party stands.
#ASSERT `s 2(7) the party is the promisee` TRUE `the party by whom the term is enforceable against the promisor` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(7) the party is the promisee` TRUE `the party against whom the term is enforceable by the third party` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(7) the party is the promisee` TRUE `a party in neither of those positions` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(7) the party is the promisee` FALSE `the party by whom the term is enforceable against the promisor` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(7) the party is the promisor` TRUE `the party against whom the term is enforceable by the third party` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(7) the party is the promisor` TRUE `the party by whom the term is enforceable against the promisor` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(7) the party is the promisor` TRUE `a party in neither of those positions` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(7) the party is the promisor` FALSE `the party against whom the term is enforceable by the third party` EQUALS NOTHING
